From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Fri, 07 Aug 2026 16:21:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: restore HT/VHT width caps in CSA fallback

hostapd_event_ch_switch() sets and clears the HT40 and VHT width
capability bits based on the width of the switched channel. The CSA
fallback path restarts the interface instead of performing a real
channel switch, so no ch_switch event fires and a previously
cleared bit is never set back, leaving the AP advertising a
narrower width than it operates. Restore the bits from the hardware
mode before the restart.

The iface->current_mode dereferences are guarded and a missing mode
is treated as capable: the ubus switch_chan force path arms
switch_chan_fallback_cb() as an eloop timeout that is never
cancelled, and hostapd_cleanup_iface_partial() sets current_mode to
NULL on disable. The VHT restore is inert in this tree, since the
bandwidth switch above already sets VHT160 unguarded for the
160 MHz case; the HT40 restore is the new behavior.

Based-on-work-by: StanleyYP Wang <StanleyYP.Wang@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 src/ap/hostapd.c |    9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -5035,6 +5035,15 @@ hostapd_switch_channel_fallback(struct h
 		break;
 	}
 
+	if ((!iface->current_mode ||
+	     (iface->current_mode->ht_capab & HT_CAP_INFO_SUPP_CHANNEL_WIDTH_SET)) &&
+	    freq_params->bandwidth > 20)
+		iface->conf->ht_capab |= HT_CAP_INFO_SUPP_CHANNEL_WIDTH_SET;
+	if ((!iface->current_mode ||
+	     (iface->current_mode->vht_capab & VHT_CAP_SUPP_CHAN_WIDTH_160MHZ)) &&
+	    freq_params->bandwidth == 160)
+		iface->conf->vht_capab |= VHT_CAP_SUPP_CHAN_WIDTH_160MHZ;
+
 	iface->freq = freq_params->freq;
 	iface->conf->channel = freq_params->channel;
 	iface->conf->secondary_channel = freq_params->sec_channel_offset;
